 pavilions and the higher central pavilion with its stone portal, all under slate hips - faces south onto the forecourt; the glazed Sculpture Street runs its whole length behind it, then Indrio's white wing with its glazed front to the park, the park's trees and the lake. Still guessed: the pavilions' sizes and heights, the window rhythm, the roof forms, how far the new wing runs."}